{"bill":{"id":"119-s-1282","congress":119,"billType":"s","billNumber":"1282","title":"Rural Development Hospital Technical Assistance Program Act of 2025","introducedDate":"2025-04-03","latestActionDate":"2025-04-03","latestActionText":"Read twice and referred to the Committee on Agriculture, Nutrition, and Forestry.","policyArea":"Agriculture and Food","subjects":[],"sponsorBioguideId":"R000605","cosponsorBioguideIds":["W000800","H001046","B001319","S001150","H001079","M001243","O000174"],"committeeCodes":[],"committeeNames":[],"officialSummary":"Rural Development Hospital Technical Assistance Program Act of 2025 This bill provides statutory authority for the Rural Hospital Technical Assistance Program within the Department of Agriculture (USDA). Under the bill, USDA must establish and maintain (directly or by grant, contract, or cooperative agreement) a program to help eligible hospital facilities in rural areas (i.e., an area with a population of 50,000 inhabitants or less). The program must provide tailored technical assistance and training to hospital facilities to identify development needs for maintaining essential health care services and support action plans for financial, operational, and quality improvement projects to meet these needs. Development needs include (1) constructing, expanding, and modernizing health care facilities; (2) increasing telehealth capabilities; and (3) acquiring or upgrading health care information systems (e.g., electronic health records). The program must also provide technical assistance and training to help hospital facilities to better manage their financial and business strategies and identify, and apply for assistance from, USDA loan and grant programs. In selecting eligible hospital facilities to participate in the program, USDA must give priority to borrowers of loans and recipients of grants from certain USDA rural assistance programs. USDA must also submit an annual report to Congress on the progress and results of the program.","congressDotGovUrl":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/senate-bill/1282","source":"congress","sourceUrl":"https://www.govinfo.gov/bulkdata/BILLSTATUS/119/s/BILLSTATUS-119s1282.xml","fetchedAt":"2026-07-29T01:30:02.260Z"},"classification":{"billId":"119-s-1282","plainSummary":"This bill formally establishes a technical assistance program within the Department of Agriculture to help rural hospitals (in areas with 50,000 or fewer residents) improve their operations and finances. The program would provide training and support to help these hospitals modernize facilities, expand telehealth, upgrade information systems, and navigate USDA loan and grant programs. Priority would go to hospitals already participating in certain USDA rural assistance programs, and USDA would report annually to Congress on the program's results.","industries":[{"industry":"health-providers","confidence":0.95,"rationale":"The bill directly targets rural hospitals, providing them with technical assistance, training, and support for operational and financial improvements."},{"industry":"telecom","confidence":0.6,"rationale":"The program explicitly includes increasing telehealth capabilities as a development need, which would affect broadband and telecommunications infrastructure providers serving rural hospitals."},{"industry":"tech","confidence":0.55,"rationale":"The bill addresses acquiring and upgrading health care information systems including electronic health records, which would involve technology vendors and IT service providers."},{"industry":"construction","confidence":0.5,"rationale":"The program covers technical assistance for constructing, expanding, and modernizing health care facilities, which would involve construction and engineering firms."}],"method":"llm","model":"claude-sonnet-4-5","inputHash":"a032d831c390b7e01fbc5dd3","classifiedAt":"2026-07-30T02:49:38.023Z"},"plain":{"whatItDoes":"This bill would provide statutory authority for the Rural Hospital Tech